# The Dockerfile COPYs certs/ and the Claude Code policy file — keep everything
# else out of the build context so config edits do not invalidate layers and
# secrets never reach the daemon. The policy file is deliberately IN the
# context: it is baked into the image at build time (see the Dockerfile), so a
# policy change is a rebuild, which an agent inside the container cannot do.
*
!certs/
!config/claude/managed-settings.json
